Author: b <a@b>
Date:   Mon Oct 5 20:46:28 2026 -0700

    REFACTOR-0003: Manager keeps one list of Employees
    
    Manager kept one array per role and looped over each one in every
    operation, so adding a role meant a new array and a new loop in every
    operation. It now keeps one Employee[] and asks each report the same
    question, whether that report is one person or a manager with a team of
    their own. The recursion that only the managers' loop had is now just
    what a Manager's answer is.
    
    Because Manager asks its reports for getTotalSalary() instead of reading
    their salary field, salary is now private. Reports are added with add()
    rather than pushed onto a per-role array, so the chart also prints them
    in the order they were added, not grouped by role.

